# The string is made flat once, in front of the loop and under the handler of the try block. Nothing in the loop allocates then: no block of it has a handler.
# IR-LABEL: function f1 name="commas"
# IR: Jump -> next [[entry]]()
# IR-NEXT: b1({{*}}):
# IR-NEXT: LoopHint
# IR-NOT: handler=
# IR-NOT: LoopHint
# IR: role=CatchHandler
# IR: [[entry]]() handler=
# IR-NEXT: flatstring = FlattenString v0
# IR-NEXT: Jump -> next b1(

# The loop is the one that stands outside a try block: eight characters a turn off one address, no poll, no test of the string.
# CHECK-LABEL: steps by 8
# CHECK-NOT: LoopHint
# CHECK: Int32 b@{{*}} = Load8Z(b@{{*}}, ControlDependent|ReadsImmutable|Reads:characters8
# REPEAT: turn = 1..7
# CHECK: Int32 b@{{*}} = Load8Z(b@{{*}}, offset = %(turn), ControlDependent|ReadsImmutable|Reads:characters8
# END REPEAT
# CHECK-NOT: LoopHint
# CHECK-LABEL: end of loop
# CHECK-NOT: Terminal|ExitsSideways{{*}}:LoopHint
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# Eight characters cost 27 instructions: a comparison with memory and a branch each, the address, the counter and its branch, and what keeps the count.
# X64: instructions: 27, patchpoints: 8, rare instructions: 13
# ARM64: instructions: 36, patchpoints: 8
